<title>FRANCE: Porsche to stick by full sick pay-out.</title>
<headline>Porsche to stick by full sick pay-out.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of German sportscar maker Porsche AG, Wendelin Wiedeking, said on Tuesday the company would maintain the current policy of paying 100 percent of gross wages for sick days.</p>
<p>A new German law took effect on Tuesday that allows companies to cut sick-pay benefits to 80 percent of wages from the current level of 100 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
